# Cloudflare Workers static-assets routing. First-match-wins; static files
# take precedence.
#
# The SPA fallback (`/* -> /index.html 200`) that used to live here has been
# REMOVED. On Workers with `[assets] not_found_handling = "single-page-
# application"` (see wrangler.toml), the assets binding itself serves
# /index.html for any unmatched path — the _redirects rule is redundant, and
# Cloudflare's validator rejects it as an infinite loop (after its automatic
# .html + /index stripping, /index.html re-matches /*, so it flags the loop
# and refuses the deployment).
#
# Rule status codes must be one of 200/301/302/303/307/308 — anything else
# is silently dropped.

# NO TRAILING SLASHES — enforce via 301, not convention. `:splat` captures
# the rest of the URL after the leading `/`. The trailing-slash form is
# always the pre-image, the clean form is the target.
/*/                       /:splat                301
